{{!-- What the container holds. The rows are siblings in the same actor's item collection, each
      naming this container in `system.container` — so this tab is a filtered view of the actor's
      items, and it is empty for a container with no actor (a compendium entry, or one sitting in
      the world Items directory), which can hold nothing.

      No heading over the list: the tab is already called Contents, and a zone head saying ITEMS
      under it named the same thing twice in a window with one list in it.

      The empty line IS the invitation. "This container is empty" and "Drag an item here" were two
      lines saying one thing, one of them only when there was nothing to say it about.

      A row is `draggable` — the class v14 binds dragging to (`ux/drag-drop.mjs`), never the HTML
      attribute — so a held thing can be dragged back out onto the character sheet. Core's own
      item-sheet handler only knows how to drag an ActiveEffect, so `item-sheet.js#_onDragStart`
      puts the sibling Item on the transfer. --}}
<section class="tab {{tabs.contents.cssClass}}" data-group="primary" data-tab="contents">
    <ol class="cairn-plain-list">
        {{#each contents as |item|}}
        <li class="cairn-slot draggable" data-item-id="{{item.id}}"
            {{#unless @last}}data-ink="hline" data-ink-seed="held-{{item.id}}" data-ink-w="0.9" data-ink-a="0.42" data-ink-at="bottom"{{/unless}}>
            <span class="cairn-slot-body">
                <span class="cairn-item-name-and-tags">
                    <span class="cairn-item-title">{{item.name}}</span>
                    {{> "systems/cairn2e/templates/parts/item-tags.hbs" system=item.system}}
                </span>
            </span>
            <span class="cairn-item-controls">
                <a data-action="contentRemove" data-tooltip="{{localize 'CAIRN.TakeOut'}}"><i class="fas fa-arrow-up-from-bracket"></i></a>
            </span>
        </li>
        {{else}}
        <li class="cairn-empty">{{localize 'CAIRN.ContainerDropHint'}}</li>
        {{/each}}
    </ol>
</section>
